      "content": "Supporters argue that clean energy legislation is economically essential for creating green jobs and reducing expensive fossil fuel dependence, while critics contend it imposes undue taxes on consumers and small businesses that stifle innovation. The opposition raises legitimate concerns about grid reliability and phase-in timelines, which are serious policy challenges rather than mere political stalling. Ultimately, the debate hinges on whether immediate structural changes to the energy infrastructure can be managed without sacrificing economic stability during the transition.",
